{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>One wagon for two of the princes.</b> As a sign of brotherhood between them, through which they would be worthy that the Shechinah dwell among them, as it says: וַיְהִי בִישֻׁרוּן מֶלֶךְ בְּהִתְאַסֵּף רָאשֵׁי עָם יַחַד (Deuteronomy 33:5) — the opposite of: חָלַק לִבָּם עַתָּה יֶאשָׁמוּ (Hosea 10:2)."], :book :numbers, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:38:52.726831494Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}